==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-uk-dont cry over spilt milk.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

===Proverb===
'''[[don't]] [[cry]] over [[spilt]] [[milk]]'''

# {{idiom}} It is no use worrying about things that cannot be [[rectified]].

====Synonyms====
* [[spilt milk]]
* [[no use crying over spilt milk]]

====Translations====
{{trans-top|it's no use worrying about what cannot be rectified}}
* Chinese: [[覆水難收]], [[覆水难收]] (fù shuǐ nán shōu)
* Czech: [[neplač nad rozlitým mlékem]]
* Finnish: [[ei kannata itkeä kaatunutta maitoa]]
* Italian: [[non piangere sul latte versato]]; [[inutile piangere sul latte versato]]
{{trans-mid}}
* Japanese: [[覆水盆に返らず]] (ふくすいぼんにかえらず, fukusui bon ni kaerazu)
* Portuguese: [[não chore sobre o leite derramado]]
* Russian: [[о пролитом молоке не плачут]] (o prolítom moloké ne pláčut)
* Spanish: [[no llorar sobre la leche derramada]], [[no llorar por la leche derramada]]
* Swedish: [[gråt inte över spilld mjölk]]
{{trans-bottom}}

{{checktrans-top}}
* {{ttbc|French}}: Il ne faut pas pleurer sur le lait renversé. The origin may be found in a fable by [[w:Jean de La Fontaine|Jean de La Fontaine]], ''la laitière et le pot au lait'' (the milkmaid and the milkpot) ; but the poet borrowed themes from [[w:Aesop|Aesop]].
